# BUKLOD Main — Single Canonical Source

This rule is mandatory for every BUKLOD Main edit, regardless of chat, prompt, branch, task name, restore request, or release request.

## Canonical local workspace

Default Windows workspace:

`%USERPROFILE%\BUKLOD_WORKSPACE`

Only this folder is the writable BUKLOD Main working copy:

`%USERPROFILE%\BUKLOD_WORKSPACE\SOURCE\BUKLOD-MAIN`

The expected Git remote is:

`https://github.com/faust-0612/BUKLOD-Rork.git`

All Downloads copies, ZIP extractions, R31/R40 snapshots, V16/INNER/RESTORE/FINAL/NEW copies, recovery folders, temporary clones, release staging folders, and other BUKLOD-Rork directories are **read-only reference/recovery sources**, never normal edit roots.

## Before any edit

Before changing source, the agent must verify:

1. repository root is the canonical SOURCE path above;
2. `.buklod-local-canonical.json` exists at repository root;
3. marker `canonical_source` resolves to the current repository root;
4. Git remote `origin` is the expected BUKLOD-Rork repository;
5. current branch and `git status` are known;
6. no unrelated dirty changes will be overwritten.

If any check fails, do not edit that copy. Preserve/reconcile work into the canonical SOURCE instead.

## One app, one editable repository

For BUKLOD Main:

> ONE APP → ONE CANONICAL FOLDER → ONE GIT REPOSITORY → MANY CHATS/BRANCHES ALLOWED → ONE RELEASE PATH.

Multiple prompts are allowed. Multiple branches are allowed. A second editable BUKLOD Main clone is not allowed.

## Recovery material

R31/R40 and other approved recovery assets belong under:

`%USERPROFILE%\BUKLOD_WORKSPACE\RECOVERY\R31_R40`

Recovery files are protected reference material. If a valid newer or missing delta exists there or in another old copy, forward-port only the required delta into canonical SOURCE. Never resume feature development inside the recovery copy.

## Release path

Never deploy BUKLOD Main directly from Downloads, ZIP extracts, backups, recovery folders, ad-hoc clones, or feature branches.

Canonical web release entry point:

`scripts\RUN_CANONICAL_WEB_RELEASE.ps1`

It must operate through:

`%USERPROFILE%\BUKLOD_WORKSPACE\RELEASE\WEB\current`

Release staging is disposable and must never become an editing source.

## Zero-regression merge behavior

- Never whole-file overwrite newer working code with an older snapshot merely to recover one feature.
- Reconcile the smallest required delta.
- Preserve unrelated completed features and protections.
- R31/R40 approved character/recovery contracts remain protected unless the product owner explicitly supersedes them.
- Current standalone Focus App doors/integrations must not be removed merely because their standalone implementation lives elsewhere.

## Completion rule

A commit/build/deploy command is not completion.

For release-affecting changes use:

`EDIT → QA → WEB BUILD → DEPLOY/PREVIEW → VISIBLE LIVE VERIFICATION → NEXT PHASE`

If local path identity is uncertain, stop destructive work. Do not guess which clone is canonical.
